+**Argument** [AI reading; each step cites its Lean, and the joining of the steps is argued]. Premises:
+
 - (P1) Held de se, acting presupposes that one's own continuation has significance ([§4.1](#decomposition)).
-- (P2) The self whose continuation is presupposed is a line under a class on the root ([§4.5](#condition-on-the-root)), and that class is constant: a regularity of its own.
-- (P3) One's line runs through its conditions: one's next stage is conditioned through what one takes in and affects.
+- (P2) The self whose continuation is presupposed is a line under a class on the root ([§4.5](#condition-on-the-root)), and that class is constant up to the net's end: a regularity of its own, whose line ends only where the net itself ends.
+- (P3) One's line runs through the conditions one affects.
+- (P4) The class of one's line holds one's effects: everything one conditions is alike to oneself.
 
 Steps:
 
 1. *Need does not reach the future.* Over flows in which only active formations give, a formation active at no step of the stretch a continuation is read across is needed only where nothing lets that continuation go on (`Flow.needs_iff_none_of_inactive`). Read with time, the feeding closure holds, besides its formation, only what gives by then (`Flow.gives_of_withinFeedingUpTo`), and read across every step it can overreach (`Overlapping.closure_overreaches`) ([§4.3](#r-need-and-feeding-read-with-time)). So the future is reached, if at all, along a line, not along need.
-2. *A line goes on past a member's end.* Under a coarser class, what continues an occurrence at which a finer line ends is reached (`«过亡而续»`). In the witness of two family lines that share nothing, a family line is narrower than the one (`TwoLines.between`) and constant, since every family line there goes on without end (`TwoLines.family_constant`), and it carries the line with its core through each birth while each member's line ends (`TwoLines.core_through_birth`); every line stays within its family (`TwoLines.line_in_family`), so even the line under the one from one family's first birth does not reach the other's (`TwoLines.other_line_outside`; [01](01-ROOT.md#r-the-source-texts-test-systems)). In time, self-concern alone is kin-shaped.
-3. *The class must hold the conditions the line runs through.* In the shared-condition witness, a class holding both families' members without the condition reaches no member of the other family (`SharedCondition.affecting_member_outside`).
-4. *Through a condition one affects, the line reaches those it later feeds.* Under the one, the line from the first family's first member reaches the second family's member two generations on, through the condition its members affect (`SharedCondition.affecting_reaches_other`), and through a common cause it reaches none (`SharedCondition.fed_outside`). A constant class holding a stage of the condition with a member holds the third thing's stage that the condition feeds alike with what the member conditions next (`ThirdFed.constant_takes_third`). What only affects the condition can be left out (`ThirdAffects.finer_class_reaches`).
+2. *A line goes on past a member's end.* Under a coarser class, what continues an occurrence at which a finer line ends is reached (`«过亡而续»`). In the witness of two family lines that share nothing, a family line is narrower than the one (`TwoLines.between`) and constant, since every family line there goes on without end (`TwoLines.family_constant`), and it carries the line with its core through each birth while each member's line ends (`TwoLines.core_through_birth`); every line stays within its family (`TwoLines.line_in_family`), so even the line under the one from one family's first birth does not reach the other's (`TwoLines.other_line_outside`; [01](01-ROOT.md#r-the-source-texts-test-systems)). In a finite net, where no family goes on without end, a family's class is still constant up to the net's end and the organism's is not (`FiniteFamilies`, above). In time, self-concern alone is kin-shaped.
+3. *The class must hold one of the conditions the line passes* (`«所经必同»`). The shared-condition witness is a case: a class holding both families' members without the condition reaches no member of the other family (`SharedCondition.affecting_member_outside`).
+4. *What one's class holds with one, it carries on to all that follows.* Under P2 and P4, everything downstream of one's acts lies on one's line, and so does everything downstream of whatever one's class holds with one (`«至终常闭则后皆续»`, `«至终常闭则所及皆及»`). The witnesses read narrowly:
+   - Under the one, the line from the first family's first member reaches the second family's member two generations on, through the condition its members affect (`SharedCondition.affecting_reaches_other`), and through a common cause it reaches none (`SharedCondition.fed_outside`).
+   - A constant class holding a stage of the condition with a member holds the third thing's stage that the condition feeds alike with what the member conditions next (`ThirdFed.constant_takes_third`).
+   - What only affects the condition can be left out (`ThirdAffects.finer_class_reaches`).
+   - In a finite net the parts hold together: the class holding the families with their condition, narrower than the one, reaches the second family past the first member's end (`FiniteSharedCondition`, above).
 
-*Conclusion.* Under P1–P3, one's concern for one's own continuation reaches what the conditions one's line runs through later feed, across lines and past one's own end, in general where the open form of steps 3–4 holds. The witnesses show the parts apart, not together: going on past a member's end where nothing crosses between lines (`TwoLines`, `LineOfDescent`), and reaching across lines through an affected condition where no member's end is modelled (`SharedCondition`, `ThirdAffects`, `ThirdFed`), the shared-condition reach under the one, whose constancy is not shown there. It needs no step of invariance and does not choose the one. Steps 1 and 2 are general laws or exact witnesses. Steps 3 and 4 are shown in witnesses only, and their general form, that a constant class holding a member with the conditions its line runs through takes in what they feed, is open ([Open](#open)).
+*Conclusion.* Under P1–P4, one's concern for one's own continuation reaches everything downstream of what one conditions (`«至终常闭则所及皆及»`): across lines where the conditions one affects feed them, and past one's own end. That is a law, not only a reading of witnesses. Its parts, which `TwoLines` and `SharedCondition` show apart, hold together in `FiniteSharedCondition`. It needs no step of invariance and does not choose the one. Given the regularity of P2, P4 is equivalent to everything downstream of one's acts being alike to oneself (`«至终常类之闭当且仅当后皆同类»`), and what is alike to oneself downstream lies on one's line from there (`«至终常闭则后皆续»`). So the reach rests on one premise, holding one's effects, carried on by the regularity. The regularity does real work: without it, holding one's effects gives nothing beyond the first step (`Inconstant`), and without P4 the regularity gives nothing beyond the class (`Unclosed`).
 
 *What the path does not reach.* Each center counting from another's standpoint beyond its part as a condition. What affects one's conditions without being fed by them, counted as more than a cause. Present beings beyond every closure. Whatever no chain joins. These remain the step's.
 
 *Where it can be denied.*
 
-- **P2 is the crux.** A constant class is one under which no line ends after its first step (`«有常则相续不尽»`), so P2 asks that the line one's acts keep going be endless, which is not shown. A class under which some line ends is not constant (`«有亡之续则不有常»`): the organism's class fails P2, and under it nothing of the self follows its end, but its failing does not single that class out. In the descent that ends no line goes on without end under any relation (`LineOfDescent.Last.never_unending`), so there no class under which anything continues is constant, the one included (an inference from these laws that no landed theorem states); the family line meets P2 in `TwoLines` only because its generations go on without end (`TwoLines.family_constant`). Denying P2 is coherent, since one can presuppose the significance of a line that ends, and the path does not refute it. The question it leaves, put to philosophers in the [review packet](../review/README.md): *in acting, does one presuppose the significance of a line that ends, or of the regularity one's acts keep going?*
+- **P2 and P4 are the crux.**
+  - Constancy itself lets no line end after its first step (`«有常则相续不尽»`). So in a net where every line ends no class under which anything continues is constant, the one included. That is an inference from the law; the finite witnesses show it for the one (`FiniteFamilies.one_not_constant`, `FiniteSharedCondition.one_not_constant`). P2 asks for constancy up to the net's end instead. That condition does tell a family's class, and the class holding the families with their condition, from the organism's.
+  - The organism's class fails P2 wherever its last stage conditions anything (`«亡而网续则不至终有常»`): its line ends while what it conditions goes on, so it is no regularity of its own. Denying P2 is coherent, since one can presuppose the significance of a line that ends.
+  - Denying P4 is also coherent: one can hold only some of one's effects as one's own. But the effects that are one's own later stages are themselves conditioned through what one takes in, so such a partial holding draws its line by the identity in question [AI reading].
+
+  The questions the path leaves, put to philosophers in the [review packet](../review/README.md): *in acting, does one presuppose the significance of a line that ends, or of the regularity one's acts keep going?* And *are one's effects one's own, in the sense of whose losses count, not of what one answers for?*
 - **P3 is a correspondence.** The laws of renewal support it ([04](04-LIFE.md#r-generation-is-replenishment)), but it is not shown for actual selves. Nor is it shown that the actual net is joined, or in which direction.
 
